  "details": "I am trying to build a VRChat world in a new project, setup using VCC. Im on:\n\n1) Unity 2022.3.22f1\n\n2) VRChat SDK 3.10.3 \n\n3) VRChat package Resolver Tool 0.1.29  \n\nI'm trying to build for iOS, Android & Windows. Android and Windows work as expected, but when trying to build for iOS I get the following errors:\n\nPackages\\com.valenvrc.security_keypad\\Runtime\\Scripts\\KeyPadDataSaver.cs(91,30): error CS0115: 'KeyPadDataSaver.OnPlayerDataStorageExceeded(VRCPlayerApi)': no suitable method found to override\n\nPackages\\com.valenvrc.security_keypad\\Runtime\\Scripts\\KeyPadDataSaver.cs(97,30): error CS0115: 'KeyPadDataSaver.OnPlayerDataStorageWarning(VRCPlayerApi)': no suitable method found to override\n\nWhile the *package* throwing the error is Valens Security Keypad, the actual issue seems to be that the VRChat iOS SDK doesn't seem to have the appropriate methods to override that it does on Windows and Android. Can these please be added to the iOS SDK?\n\nI have already reported this to the package creator (Valen) and they have pointed me here as the bug is that the method is missing in the iOS VRChat SDK.",
